    finishes; the forget variant finishes and removes the record), a_local_only_forget_leaves_no_record_behind,
    a_local_only_forget_that_cannot_record_removes_nothing. All three fail on the old code.

    F14-2 (minor): "ordinal" in the plugin is -ceq - Test-ReviewerMatch and Resolve-CoordinatorIdentity
    compare the provider (and a named model) case-sensitively, the engine with -eq. The provider stays
    case-sensitive (as C3's -Require matcher); the doc comments say so; the engine comparisons use
    eq_ignore_ascii_case. Test coordinator_provider_is_case_sensitive_the_engine_is_not.

